    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "The three-year UKSPF extension would continue funding programmes that explicitly target social fabric and civic pride, which supports community cohesion. However, the subsequent pivot to mandatory National Service raises real doubts: evidence suggests compulsion undermines genuine volunteering spirit, and the funding redistribution would disadvantage the most deprived communities that UKSPF was designed to help.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether mandatory participation in a National Service scheme generates genuine civic engagement and inter-group trust, or produces resentment and shallow compliance, is the decisive empirical question \u2014 and the evidence from comparable schemes (NCS) is negative.",
